# Camel Case Preference

- Prefer `camelCase` for variables, params, props, local state, and helper names.
- Prefer `PascalCase` only for React components, types, interfaces, and classes.
- Avoid introducing new `snake_case` names in app code when a `camelCase` name works.
- Keep `snake_case` only when preserving external contracts, such as backend payload fields, database columns, RPC params, or established URL/query keys.
- When an external contract uses `snake_case`, map it at the boundary and keep the rest of the component logic in `camelCase`.

```tsx
// Avoid in component code
const workload_id = row.workload_id;

// Prefer
const workloadId = row.workload_id;
```
